.TH GIT-DELETE-WORKTREE 1 "2026-09-29" "" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-delete-worktree \- delete a worktree and its local branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git delete-worktree
[\fIworktree-name\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
.br
.B git delete-worktree
(\fB\-l\fR|\fB\-\-list\fR)
.br
.B git delete-worktree
\fB\-h\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete a Git worktree directory and the local branch checked out there.
If no worktree name is given, the current worktree is used.
The name is the worktree directory name, not a full path.
.PP
The script reads the branch's configured upstream and asks that remote
whether the branch is still there, using
.BR "git ls-remote --heads" .
A remote-tracking ref left in the local repository is not treated as proof.
The script does not fetch and does not update remote-tracking refs.
.PP
Deletion asks for an extra confirmation when the upstream branch is missing,
the local branch is ahead of it, the remote tip is not in this repository,
the remote cannot be checked, or the branch has no upstream and its commits
are not on any remote.
.B \-\-force
skips that prompt and still prints the upstream.
The remote branch is not deleted.
.PP
Protected branches (main, master, develop, development) ask for confirmation
before that upstream check.
Deleting the current worktree without
.B \-\-force
prints the unpushed-commit warning and exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Delete without confirmation prompts.
.TP
.B \-h
Show the script's usage text.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List worktrees with their branches, upstreams, and paths.
.SH NOTES
.B git delete-worktree \-\-help
and
.B man git-delete-worktree
show this manual.
Both require
.B git-delete-worktree
on
.B PATH
and this page on the manual path.
.PP
A shell alias whose value starts with
.B !
does not receive
.BR \-\-help .
Git prints the alias and exits.
.B git delete-worktree \-h
still runs the script.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR git-worktree (1),
.BR git-branch (1)
